X:1
T:Megher Kole Rod Hesechhe
C:Rabindranath Tagore
S:notes: data/raw_data/midi/rs001397.mid (Geetabitan, arranged by Anjan Ganguly), violin track
S:lyrics: data/raw_data/text/lyrics/rs001397.txt (Geetabitan transliteration)
S:alignment: data/raw_data/swaralipi/rs001397.pdf (Geetabitan swaralipi)
N:Notes quantized to 16ths, pitch bends applied (scripts/midi_to_ktab.py read_tracks). Sa = C, C major; the MIDI's A# (bars 56 82 98 128) is a passing note where the swaralipi has a held Pa/Dha melisma.
N:Form played by the MIDI: sthayi, then its first line (Megher kole ... Aaha haha haa) again; antara (its first two lines twice); sthayi first line; sanchari twice; abhog (its first two lines twice); sthayi; its first line to end.
N:Where the MIDI's rhythm inside a matra differs from the swaralipi (e.g. bar 2 G A2 B B2, bars 41 49 113 121 d2 c d2 e) the MIDI is followed; syllables are placed where the swaralipi starts them. "chuti" in the lyrics file is written chhu-ti both times, as the swaralipi has it.
N:Syllables placed on the notes as in the swaralipi; one swaralipi matra = one quarter note, one half-bar of 3 matras = one 3/4 bar.
